{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"WAVE 3 - SOURCING (in progress, no reviews dispatched). 20 plans to be sourced from OUTSIDE rebar, because Wave 1 measures 4 reviewers on ONE Python codebase in ONE house style written by authors who had the reviewer's own criteria in front of them - every Wave 1 number is entangled with that. Rules: epics only (BUGS EXCLUDED - a bug report is not a plan), substantial (4,000+ chars of plan content; Wave 1 runs 11,000-85,000), publicly readable, deliberate non-Python language spread (Java, Ruby, NextJS/TypeScript required), and heavy UI emphasis because rebar's corpus is a CLI/library/reconciler with essentially no UI - Compound Engineering's design-lens persona has DECLINED TO ACTIVATE on every Wave 1 run for lack of UI content, so an entire arm of the instrument has never fired. Code grounding IS available for Wave 3: a local checkout is materialized at a PINNED SHA contemporaneous with the issue (not today's HEAD - a plan reviewed against a tree that already implements it scores as nonsense), so all 4 arms read the same code, matching Wave 1's setup. Sourcing runs as 3 disjoint slices: Nava/Jira (navasage.atlassian.net + navapbc org), Java/JVM external OSS (Kafka KIPs, Flink FLIPs, Cassandra CEPs, Kotlin KEEPs), and non-JVM external OSS UI-first (USWDS, GOV.UK, Carbon, Primer, Radix, Rails/Hotwire, framework RFC repos). Best Nava seam identified: OSCER (Ruby, state Medicaid system) and the Strata SDKs (strata-sdk-rails Ruby, strata-sdk-case-management TypeScript, strata-unemployment benefits portal, bao-nguyen-strata-java-sdk). An SDK is an unusually good review target because its plans must reason about a public contract and downstream consumers. Pool is capped at roughly half Nava so the wave does not rebuild the monoculture it exists to break. Internal Jira material carries ticket keys/titles/descriptions/ACs but NOT personal names."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789001204949473001,"uuid":"c1bf98b7-f096-41f5-88e1-6bb2a266a4df"}